            <div xml:id="d650">

                <pb facs="0640" n="628" sameAs="frus:frus1937v01/pg628"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4 Steering Committee/511: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Mr. Norman H. Davis at
                        London</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-04-21T16:00:00-05:00">April 21, 1937—4 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your April 16, 2 p.m. I consider the progress made in the conversation you report
                    to be highly satisfactory.</p>
                <p>With regard to our taking up with Italy the matter of their not departing from
                    the provisions of the 1936 Naval Treaty, I would see no-objection to our doing
                    so if you were to recommend such an approach.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
